  "id": "activity-cycle",
  "term": "activity cycle",
  "definition": "Activity cycle, in this context, refers to the full 24-hour pattern of how a person’s day is divided among physical activity, sedentary behavior, and sleep. The idea emphasizes that time spent in these behaviors is interconnected, so changing one part of the day affects the others.",
